CONSEQUENCE: Phi(v) = m_0 (2-adic), but the REAL limit is
  Phi_R(v) = m_0 - lim (2^l/3^h) T^l(m_0),  which is a DIFFERENT number.

At accelerated endpoints l = S_N, h = N:  (2^{S_N}/3^N) m_N = 2^{-Delta_N} m_N
and by the drift identity m_N = m_0 2^{Delta_N + E_N}, so
  Phi_R(u^(S_N)) = m_0 (1 - 2^{E_N}),   E_N = sum_{j<N} log2(1+1/(3 m_j)) .

